++### Setting-by-Setting Technical Paragraphs (Workflow Transition Studio & Repo Bindings)
++
++- **name:** The user-defined identifier assigned to the workflow hook (such as `qa-done-gate` or `enforce-pr-link`). Appears on pipeline transition cards, dry-run evaluation outputs, and timeline rejection entries.
++- **from_state:** The initial state of the card before transition (e.g. `In Progress`). Selecting `null` creates a wildcard rule matching transitions originating from any state into `to_state`.
++- **to_state:** The protected destination state (e.g. `Done`). The card cannot land in this state until all attached synchronous validators pass and all asynchronous agent gates approve.
++- **hook_kind:** Defines the execution engine: `"sync_validator"` runs fast in-process WebAssembly checks (<25ms); `"sync_mutator"` applies deterministic property updates; `"agent_interceptor"` dispatches an asynchronous background gate to an AI model or test runner.
++- **failure_policy:** The error handling invariant. `"fail_closed"` (default) blocks the transition immediately if the helper fails, times out, or errors. `"fail_open_warn"` logs an administrative warning to the activity ledger and allows the card transition to complete.
++- **wasm_module_sha256:** The cryptographic hash of the compiled WebAssembly bytecode module executed by the `wasmtime` engine. Prevents execution of unverified or tampered binaries.
++- **agent:** The slug of the registered autonomous agent (`@reality-checker`, `@security-auditor`) assigned to evaluate asynchronous gate transitions. The attach dialog groups available agents by execution harness (`cli_pipe`, `in_app_sdk`, `remote_runner`).
++- **timeout_ms:** The maximum wall-clock execution deadline allocated to the helper (validating between 1 and 300,000 ms, defaulting to 60,000 ms for agent interceptors).
++- **allowed_mutable_fields:** A strict security allowlist restricting which issue properties a `sync_mutator` hook can modify (`labels`, `priority`, `assignees`, `start_date`, `due_date`, `cycle`, and `custom_fields.<slug>`). Project invariants strictly forbid modifying `state` or `description_markdown` to prevent recursive transition loops and content tampering.
++- **repo_slug:** The local filesystem folder name allocated to the bare Git mirror. Must be a clean lowercase alphanumeric string with hyphens.
++- **remote_url:** The external Git repository URL (e.g. `https://github.com/org/repo.git`). The server validates the URL against an anti-SSRF policy (blocking RFC 1918 private IP addresses unless explicitly allowlisted) before establishing outbound connections.
++- **default_ref:** The primary branch or ref name against which code inspection scripts, PR validation checks, and diff analyses are evaluated (default `"main"`).
++- **access_mode:** Defines how agents access repository contents: `"ro_vfs_mount"` mounts a read-only filesystem tree, while `"bare_git_tools"` allows executing read-only Git query commands.
++- **credential:** Optional secret identifier (`"workspace-pat"` or `"ssh-key"`) used to authenticate against private upstream repositories without exposing cleartext credentials to agents.
++
++### Step-by-Step Guide: Attaching Workflow Transition Hooks with Dry-Run
++
++1. **Navigate to Workflow Studio:** Open `/projects/<PROJECT_KEY>/settings/workflows`.
++2. **Select Transition Rule:** Locate the transition rule card for your target state movement (e.g. `In Progress -> Done`).
++3. **Click Attach Hook:** Click the **+ Attach Hook** button to open the Attach Workflow Hook Dialog.
++4. **Define Hook Parameters:** Specify a unique Hook Name (e.g. `reality-checker-done-gate`), select the Hook Kind (`sync_validator`, `sync_mutator`, or `agent_interceptor`), and choose the Failure Policy (`fail_closed` to block unverified tickets, or `fail_open_warn` to log warnings while allowing progress).
++5. **Select Engine or Agent:** For Wasm, choose an approved module (e.g. `check-blockers-resolved`). For Agent Interceptors, select the target Agent Definition from the dropdown; the system automatically populates the agent's real timeout (between 1 and 300,000 ms, e.g. `60000ms`). For mutators, select permitted mutable fields (`labels`, `priority`, `assignees`, `start_date`, `due_date`, `cycle`, or `custom_fields.<slug>`).
++6. **Save Hook:** Click **Attach Hook** to commit the hook to the project's transition pipeline.
++7. **Simulate in Dry-Run Drawer:** Click the **Dry-Run** button on the rule card, choose a sample ticket fixture or enter a live issue key, click **Run Dry-Run** to execute the pipeline in a simulated, non-mutating sandbox, and inspect the execution timings (e.g. `1.2ms`, `3.4ms`), returned logs, and allowed/vetoed verdicts before deploying to production.
++
++### Step-by-Step Guide: Binding Git Repositories
++
++1. **Access Repository Bindings:** Navigate to `/projects/<PROJECT_KEY>/settings/workflows` and scroll down to the Git Repository Bindings section.
++2. **Click Bind Repository:** Click **+ Bind Git Repository** to open the repository configuration drawer.
++3. **Configure Repository Details:** Enter the Repository Slug (e.g. `kanban-core`), remote repository URL (`remote_url`), default tracking branch or ref (`default_ref`, e.g. `main`), access mode (`ro_vfs_mount` or `bare_git_tools`), and optional credential binding (`workspace-pat` or `ssh-key`).
++4. **Enforce Read-Only Mirror Invariant:** The system creates a local bare Git mirror with strict read-only permissions (`:ro`). Autonomous agents can query commit trees and run `git diff` during gate reviews, but write access is impossible.
++5. **Trigger Immediate Mirror Refresh:** Click **Refresh Mirror** to perform an initial fetch and verify that commit SHAs and branch references synchronize successfully.
